WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.4 · Financial Management
Restricted and unrestricted funds

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know which money is committed to what, and show how each restricted fund is used.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Give each grant a code in your accounts.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Record spending against it and track the balance.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Keep enough flexible money for core costs.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Riverside: of £47,000 in the bank, £36,200 is restricted and £8,000 designated for the move. Little is actually free.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a funds register with balances and reporting dates.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
